    "heightBasis": "The approximately66x44m current parent and two front building-part plans control horizontal placement. The north part includes a broad lower mass;its upper tower is a photo-led9.5x9.3m reconstruction within that control. The south tower retains its raw plan. No part heights exist. The current17m parent is a generic levels-derived value and is not used as the overall cathedral height. Photo-led estimates are14.5..15.1m low aisles,22.5..27m nave,24m central front/27m gable,27.5..36.7m belfries,37.6m parapets,45.3m pale pyramid tips and46.2m finials. Right upper bell frame reaches44.2m. Openings,balcony,clocks,buttresses and all vertical stages remain approximate;no independently measured heights.",
